course: dictionary
lesson: 8194
title: Restore: bringing things back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Restore is a verb. Restores, restored and restoring show when it happens: «Power was restored after the storm.» The power had gone off, and then it came back on.
explain: Restore has three everyday meanings. It can mean to repair something so it looks or works as it did when new. It can mean to bring back something lost, like peace, power or health. It can also mean to give something back to the person who owned it.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Common cranes... nest there again after wetlands were restored.» The wetlands had been damaged, and then they were made good again. Ask: could I swap in repaired or brought back? If yes, restore probably fits.
fact: Restore means to repair something so it looks or works as it did when it was new.
fact: Restore can also mean to bring back something that was lost, like order, power or health.
fact: To restore something to a person means to give it back to them.
fact: «Common cranes», gone from Britain for about 400 years, nest there again after wetlands were restored.
fact: Phrases you will meet are restore order, restore power, restore to health, and fully restored.
exercise: «Power was restored after the storm.» What does restored mean here? | *Brought back after being lost | Made wet by the rain | Broke into small pieces | Forgotten by everyone
exercise: An old church is being restored so it looks as it did when it was built. What does restore mean here? | Sell it to a museum | Paint it a new colour and change its shape | *Repair it so it looks as it did when new | Knock it down to build something new
exercise: Which word could replace restore in: «The finder restored the wallet to its owner»? | *Returned | Stretched | Sold | Hidden
test: The doctor hopes the medicine will restore Sam to health. What does restore to health mean? | *Bring Sam back to being well | Make Sam sick | Hide Sam's medicine | Keep Sam in bed for a week
test: «Common cranes... nest there again after wetlands were restored.» What had probably happened to the wetlands before they were restored? | They had been sold to a farm | They had been moved to the sea | *They had been damaged or lost, and then made good again | They had been made bigger
exam: What does restore mean in: «We must restore the broken lamp before the show»? | *To repair it so it works again | To switch it off for ever | To hide it under the desk | To smash it into pieces
